WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.842
Semantic similarity alone is not enough for many real RAG systems.

00:00:04.842 --> 00:00:13.547
A user may ask a question that is semantically related to several documents, but some of those documents may belong to

00:00:13.547 --> 00:00:18.377
the wrong department, language, audience, tenant, or permission level.

00:00:18.377 --> 00:00:22.432
Metadata filters let us narrow the candidate set.

00:00:22.432 --> 00:00:29.127
In our example, we can filter by topic and permission before ranking the remaining vectors.

00:00:29.845 --> 00:00:32.437
This is especially important for security.

00:00:32.437 --> 00:00:41.127
If a student is only allowed to see public student-facing documents, staff-only content should not be retrieved and then

00:00:41.127 --> 00:00:44.567
hidden later. Access control belongs in the retrieval layer.

00:00:44.567 --> 00:00:47.427
Filters can also improve relevance.

00:00:47.427 --> 00:00:55.542
If we know the question is about technology, limiting search to the technology topic can reduce unrelated results.

00:00:55.542 --> 00:01:00.155
In production, metadata design is part of RAG design.
